    {
      "title": "Combine prior, visits and per-action values",
      "explanation": "At an intermediate point during search, each root action has a current visit count and an averaged value. We denote these vectors by $N_{\\mathrm{cur}}$ and $Q_{\\mathrm{cur}}$. For action $a$, the value averages leaf states from simulations that selected $a$ at $s_t$. Selection considers low visit count together with high prior and high averaged value, so previous search results influence which alternatives are explored next.",
