    {
      "title": "Convert completed visits into a policy",
      "explanation": "After the full simulation series, $N_{\\mathrm{fin}}$ and $Q_{\\mathrm{fin}}$ denote the completed per-action statistics, replacing the intermediate snapshot. For training self-play, the distribution $\\boldsymbol\\pi_t$ is proportional to root visit counts: $\\pi_t(a)\\propto N_{\\mathrm{fin}}(s_t,a)$. The learned prior guides the search; its resulting visits determine the move distribution.",
